#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:5
#: 98807f3544234e9facdacdb7391d79d7
msgid "RTL Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:7
#: 7133e7b4627344288f41404f8f9197dc
msgid "RTL mode (Return To Launch mode) navigates Copter from its current position to hover above the home position. The behavior of RTL mode can be controlled by several adjustable parameters. This page describes how to use and customize RTL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:13
#: 69ff560864fb4fff93960951debc451a
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:15
#: c23d3997fd29484e879bd928d58a485e
msgid "When RTL mode is selected, the copter will return to the home location, or if :ref:`rally points <common-rally-points>` have been setup, the closest rally point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:17
#: 727d91a8908743488c6abb3ff7ddc3d5
msgid "The copter will first rise a minimum of :ref:`RTL_CLIMB_MIN<RTL_CLIMB_MIN>` or to  :ref:`RTL_ALT_M<RTL_ALT_M>`, whichever is higher, before returning home.  The default value for :ref:`RTL_ALT_M<RTL_ALT_M>` is 15m. Under no circumstances will this altitude be below 30cm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:19
#: 3ca5d39584ba404cb15020583f6699c5
msgid "The altitude reference frame is set by either the rally point, if proceeding to one of those, or by :ref:`RTL_ALT_TYPE<RTL_ALT_TYPE>` to select relative to HOME, or Terrain. If :ref:`WP_RFND_USE<WP_RFND_USE>` = 1 and Terrain is selected, then rangefinder will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:24
#: a2e0e429b6d8455dafb6106770b17e7b
msgid "If RTL is entered close to its return point, the altitude Copter climbs to may be limited to avoid unneeded climbs and descents. The :ref:`RTL_CONE_SLOPE<RTL_CONE_SLOPE>` parameter determines the slope of an inverted cone centered on the return point. This reduces the above return altitude according to: distance from return point * :ref:`RTL_CONE_SLOPE<RTL_CONE_SLOPE>`. So if the mode is entered 10m from the return point, using the default slope of \"3\", then the altitude rise would be limited to 30m before returning. It may be less depending on the other parameters, but not higher. If the slope were set to \"0.5\", then the initial climb would be no higher than 5m altitude before proceeding to the return point. A value of \"0\" disables this limit. \"0.5\" is the minimum slope. Again, 2m is the minimum return altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:26
#: 8c1a701b1e7d4dae9e79843467bf1d10
msgid "If an :ref:`altitude fence <common-geofencing-landing-page>` has been enabled, the RTL climb/return altitude will be limited to be below the fence's maximum altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:28
#: ed214df382544b35889f58ab8ea9c428
msgid "RTL mode requires a reliable position estimate to work properly, most commonly provided by GPS and compass. Default prearm checks will ensure a 3D GPS lock with sufficient HDOP is acquired and your mag is working as expected prior to arming, if required by the selected mode and configuration during arming (ie STABILIZE could be armed without a reliable position and a switch into RTL would be refused without it). When using non-default arming checks, make sure you do have a sufficient GPS lock and / or a reliable position estimate for RTL to perform as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:30
#: 7ddfcbbe845f4082953496b7e75fdfc0
msgid "RTL will command the copter to return to the home position, meaning that it will return to the location where it was armed. Therefore, the home position is always supposed to be your copter's actual GPS takeoff location, unobstructed and away from people. For Copter if you get GPS lock and then ARM your copter, the home position is the location the copter was in when it was armed. This means if you execute an RTL in Copter, it will return to the location where it was armed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:40
#: 5550e666ed9149468607352125b09683
msgid "In RTL mode the autopilot uses a barometer which measures air pressure as the primary means for determining altitude (\"Pressure Altitude\") and if the air pressure is changing in your flight area, the copter will follow the air pressure change rather than actual altitude (unless you are within 20 feet of the ground and have SONAR installed and enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:48
#: c886474589cd47059a4d11b37911a3d7
msgid "Options (User Adjustable Parameters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:50
#: 398680ed78f644cd898c209f3bfc4c70
msgid ":ref:`RTL_ALT_M<RTL_ALT_M>`: The minimum altitude the copter will move to before returning to launch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:53
#: b008a732eda346708c06b587846695b5
msgid "Set to zero to return at the current altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:54
#: 5cb4f96c892243eaad1aac9a4c9f0f30
msgid "The return altitude can be set from 0.3 to 3000 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:55
#: 824716a7237e4915939b7bfaff5abdff
msgid "The default return altitude Default is 15 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:57
#: 0f4ffddd4e854125a1d625bd7d7fa3be
msgid ":ref:`RTL_ALT_FINAL_M<RTL_ALT_FINAL_M>`: The altitude the copter will move to at the final stage of \"Returning to Launch\" or after completing a Mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:61
#: aab52fae5a0a41a58fb0c0aaad5975b3
msgid "Set to zero to automatically land the copter. See :ref:`land-mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:62
#: 1f5afd42f13544019521e6c85cff4ee6
msgid "The final return altitude may be adjusted from 0 to 10 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:65
#: 1b4a09c370a545048d0381f11fa71568
msgid ":ref:`RTL_LOIT_TIME <RTL_LOIT_TIME>`: Time in milliseconds to hover/pause above the \"Home\" position before beginning final descent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:69
#: 3c8c6f51807047ce9f72e56fe46ad78d
msgid "The \"Loiter\" time may be adjusted from 0 to 60,000 milliseconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:71
#: a3406b9438cf4e52957f40f6164e21dd
msgid ":ref:`WP_YAW_BEHAVIOR <WP_YAW_BEHAVIOR>`: Sets how the autopilot controls the \"Yaw\" during Missions and RTL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:74
#: b7f35dc9356b4d14a816e6e91b401ac4
msgid "0 = Never change Yaw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:75
#: e8286ea024c3467e8bc565b086bbbb3f
msgid "1 = Face Next Waypoint including facing home during RTL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:76
#: d609400e9a9147aabc4d3e81a862a998
msgid "2 = Face Next Waypoint except for RTL (i.e. during RTL vehicle will remain pointed at its last heading)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:79
#: 8d79c774aae244aab374c9fb482884ec
msgid ":ref:`LAND_SPD_MS<LAND_SPD_MS>`: The descent speed for the final stage of landing in centimeters per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:83
#: de57da6c50e141078209f6aa735d3140
msgid "The landing speed is adjustable from 0.3 to 2 meters per second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:86
#: f3e5d135d4414f61a3b370fa3b08cb54
msgid ":ref:`RTL_CLIMB_MIN <RTL_CLIMB_MIN>`: The vehicle will climb at least this many meters at the first stage of the RTL.  By default this value is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:90
#: 80996f656a91439c9821e0fac10703a4
msgid ":ref:`RTL_SPEED <RTL_SPEED>`: The horizontal speed (in cm/s) at which the vehicle will return to home.  By default this value is zero meaning it will use :ref:`WP_SPD<WP_SPD>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rtl-mode.rst:95
#: 7babf54d0a004f17a870bf6c1f697292
msgid ":ref:`RTL_CONE_SLOPE <RTL_CONE_SLOPE>`: Defines the slope of an inverted cone above home which is used to limit the amount the vehicle climbs when RTL-ing from close to home. Low values lead to a wide cone meaning the vehicle will climb less, High values will lead to the vehicle climbing more."
msgstr ""

